      "parameters": {},
      "status": "drafted",
      "rule_append": "The characteristic addition is a single-storey rear lean-to framed as a shorter, independent span leaned on the main block's existing rear plate -- no new plate, chimney or second-floor framing required -- which is why the type is the cheapest way to add space to an existing First Period house rather than a composed design."
